<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">12092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Houthi fighters now hold Perim Island, the rock that sits barely three kilometres from the shipping lane at Bab al-Mandab, giving Iran's allies leverage over more than thirty-five percent of the world's oil and fuel trade, Chatham House says.</s> <s>A strait doesn't close by blockade... it closes by risk, as war-risk insurance premiums climb for every ship bound for Suez.</s> <s>Egypt's canal revenue, East African importers, and Yemenis on the coast will feel it before anyone in a Western capital does.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Forty-six thousand people fled Yemen's Red Sea coast this week as the fighting moved along the Tihama plain.</s> <s>Aid workers say many are on their second or third displacement, and the Tihama is precisely where the country's food imports come ashore, so the same families lose their homes and the route their flour travels by.</s> <s>The UN warns the offensive could draw in the wider region, and no Yemeni or Gulf outlet has yet put its own count against that figure.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Tehran is weighing something almost nobody has picked up... a system of service fees for passage through the Strait of Hormuz.</s> <s>Gulf diplomats meet Iranian counterparts in Oman on Monday, and the idea would convert a wartime chokehold into a lasting revenue arrangement, one the Gulf states themselves would then have an interest in preserving.</s> <s>Riyadh, Abu Dhabi and Doha haven't said whether they'll accept a toll on a waterway that once carried a fifth of the world's oil.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Central Intelligence Agency has released seventy-one presidential daily briefs, and the first warning about Osama bin Laden is dated February nineteen ninety-eight.</s> <s>A presidential daily brief is the highest-priority intelligence product a government produces, so the question was never what was known but what a warning with no owner actually triggers — which agency was tasked, and what became of the tasking.</s> <s>The documents landed the same week families of those killed on the eleventh of September pressed for accountability over Saudi Arabia's alleged role, a civil case they've pursued since Congress lifted Saudi immunity in twenty sixteen.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pyongyang fired ballistic missiles roughly two hundred and fifty kilometres from Wonsan, one day after five days of joint exercises by Washington, Seoul and Tokyo ended.</s> <s>That sequence is the whole mechanism — a signalling loop where each side's routine act is the other's provocation, and neither can step back without appearing to concede.</s> <s>In an inversion worth noticing, Democrats in Washington are now pressing Trump to reverse the drill cutback he ordered, while he still says he plans to meet Kim Jong Un this year.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Spain's parliament voted one hundred and sixty-eight to thirty-one to open citizenship to Sahrawis.</s> <s>Madrid governed Western Sahara until nineteen seventy-five and never completed decolonisation, and the UN still lists Spain as the territory's administering power — so more than a hundred thousand people born under Spanish rule stand to gain passports from the state that left them stateless.</s> <s>The bill has further parliamentary stages before it becomes law, God willing for the families waiting in the Tindouf camps.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Islamabad has become the channel between Riyadh and the Houthis, after Iran's foreign minister called Pakistan and then Saudi Arabia in turn.</s> <s>The Mecca pact binds nuclear-armed Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and Turkey to mutual defence, which means a widening Yemen war pulls in a nuclear state by treaty, not by choice.</s> <s>Houthi advances continue while the mediation runs.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Vladimir Putin called the presence of European troops in Ukraine, plainly, a war.</s> <s>Moscow has named Western soldiers on Ukrainian soil a red line since the twenty twenty-two invasion, and the warning lands while NATO members debate who would police any ceasefire.</s> <s>Trump has proposed one, but no country has yet volunteered its soldiers to enforce it.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Drones launched from Iraq's Maysan province struck Saudi Arabia's East-West pipeline on Thursday, and Riyadh has shut the line.</s> <s>That pipeline exists for one reason — to carry seven million barrels a day of eastern crude to the Red Sea so exports can bypass Hormuz — so with the line down and Bab al-Mandab under Houthi guns, the kingdom's bypass and its exit are gone at the same moment.</s> <s>Aramco hasn't said when pumping resumes, and diesel buyers in import-dependent economies pay first.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American consumer prices rose four tenths of a percent in August, with petrol up twenty-seven percent on the year driving a third of that gain.</s> <s>Brent crude traded near a hundred and nine dollars a barrel, pushed there by the Hormuz and Red Sea disruptions — which is how a war in the Arabian Peninsula arrives in a Kansas grocery bill.</s> <s>Markets now put eighty-seven percent odds on a Federal Reserve rate rise next week.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan taxes petrol at a hundred and fourteen rupees a litre, and Jamaat-i-Islami will march on Islamabad on the twentieth of September unless that levy goes.</s> <s>The levy is the government's main non-shareable revenue and a benchmark written into its International Monetary Fund programme, so dropping it means breaking a loan condition and keeping it means the streets.</s> <s>Ministers haven't said which they'll choose.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India is offering its instant-payment network to fellow BRICS members, a system that already clears more than two hundred and fifty billion transfers a year.</s> <s>Linking national payment rails lets sanctioned members like Russia and Iran route around the Belgium-based bank-messaging system that has carried Western financial power for half a century.</s> <s>Commerce minister Piyush Goyal urged members to settle trade in their own currencies, which is the quieter half of the same project.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bogotá and Washington have set a six-month clock on a minerals agreement covering gold, nickel, coltan and rare earths, paired with security assistance and civil-nuclear cooperation.</s> <s>What's being traded is access to the ground for a say in how Colombia's own counter-narcotics war is fought, and the country has just loosened nearly a dozen mining rules.</s> <s>China's competing position in the region, built through the port at Chancay and copper offtake deals, is the unstated other party to the deal.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Regulators approved the first drug that treats the muscle loss in spinal muscular atrophy rather than its genetic cause.</s> <s>Existing therapies keep motor neurons alive, but children who survive on them are left with muscle that never repairs — this one blocks myostatin, the protein that brakes muscle growth, so for the first time the two halves of the disease have separate treatments given together.</s> <s>The harder question is price, because newborn screening for this disorder barely exists across South Asia and much of Africa, and a fourth drug widens a gap the first three already opened.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American health officials have declared the largest cyclosporiasis outbreak ever recorded over: twelve thousand eight hundred and eighty-three people infected, two dead, traced to lettuce.</s> <s>This parasite doesn't pass between people — its eggs need days outside a host to become infectious — which means every one of those cases traces back to contaminated water touching a crop in a field in Mexico.</s> <s>Washing doesn't reliably help, so the fix is agricultural and regulatory, and the question is what actually changes before next season's harvest.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia's fires have released seventy-six million tonnes of carbon, matching the pace of twenty fifteen, when regional haze contributed to more than a hundred thousand deaths.</s> <s>Peat burns underground for weeks, releasing carbon that took centuries to accumulate, which is why these fires can't simply be put out from above.</s> <s>One of the most intense El Niño patterns on record is still building.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chemists at Rice University have turned forever-chemical waste into silver fluoride using electrical pulses.</s> <s>The pulses snap the carbon-fluorine bond, the strongest in organic chemistry and the very thing that makes these compounds persist in blood and groundwater for decades, and the freed fluoride becomes a reagent industry pays for.</s> <s>It remains a laboratory demonstration, not yet a working plant.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Anthropic says a cell in Yemen used its Claude model on three weapons programmes: guidance software for a rocket, a missile with two thousand kilometres of range, and a hypersonic glide vehicle.</s> <s>The company caught it and cut the accounts off, which is the actual story — the control on missile-guidance knowledge was a vendor's abuse-detection team reading usage telemetry, not any export-control regime, because no regulator has authority to act in Yemen.</s> <s>Read it sceptically in both directions... a company's own threat report is also advertising for its safety programme.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Matt Mullenweg says he's back in control of Automattic, days after its board placed him on leave.</s> <s>WordPress runs an enormous share of the world's websites, and the open-source project's governance runs through him personally while he also runs the company that monetises it — no foundation vote, no fork that keeps the plugin ecosystem intact.</s> <s>One executive's state of mind is load-bearing infrastructure for newsrooms and small businesses who chose WordPress precisely because nobody owned it, and the board has told employees nothing beyond a single message posted on Wednesday.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>France's joint combat-aircraft programme with Germany has collapsed, after Dassault and Airbus failed to agree who leads the design and who owns the intellectual property.</s> <s>Europe has now failed twice in a generation to build a fighter together, and the last failure produced the Rafale, the Typhoon and the Gripen from one broken partnership.</s> <s>An upgraded Rafale enters service at the end of the decade, leaving Paris to keep its air force credible into the twenty-thirties alone.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>